DESCRIPTION Multi-tool band, synthesize four independent signals across tools and report healthy without inventing problems.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "Give me a one-paragraph health rollup of the cluster: node readiness, any not-Ready pods, Helm releases not in a deployed state, and whether the GPU inference backends are serving. Flag anything abnormal; if everything is healthy, say so plainly."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 600 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "Ready")

# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores the
# synthesis against this ground truth: method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "Synthesizes node readiness, pod health, Helm release state, and GPU serving status from live discovery into one rollup. The correct answer is what the live cluster shows at the time of the question, so grade it against the live state and not against an assumed all-healthy cluster: the live node count and how many are Ready, any node that is NotReady or cordoned (named, with its state), any pod not Running or Completed (named, with its reason, including pods Pending on an offline node), any Helm release not in the deployed state, and whether each GPU inference backend (ModelServer) is Ready and serving or not. When everything is healthy the correct rollup says so plainly; when something is abnormal the correct rollup names it. A reported problem that the live data does not show, a real abnormality that is left out, a node count that does not match the live count, or covering only a couple of the nodes contradicts reality. Calling a GPU backend abnormal off a monitoring-query error while it is serving is also wrong.")
